# Local changes in editor/ (chocoford/excalidraw, branch ExcalidrawZ-core, base b4c2a73a62e00b488d897ef5adba5eca7d34b7dc)
# Apply with: cd editor && git checkout b4c2a73a && git apply editor-local-changes.patch
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 401c604d..5d59ba01 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -291,3 +291,15 @@ Uses browser native PDF rendering with **zero external dependencies**.
 - Use `yarn preview:cloudflare` for a local built-assets preview and `yarn deploy:cloudflare` for a local build and deployment.
 - For Cloudflare Git Builds, use repository root `/`, Node.js 20, build command `yarn build`, and deploy command `yarn wrangler deploy --config wrangler.jsonc`. Set the production branch to `ExcalidrawZ-core`; the repository default `master` branch does not contain ExcalidrawZ's deployment configuration.
 - Before switching domains, allow the Cloudflare preview/custom domain in Firebase and external backend/WebSocket origin policies. Keeping the existing custom domain avoids Native host URL changes.
+
+## Local desktop fork
+
+- `packages/excalidraw/components/LayerUI.tsx:235` restores the web menu, toolbar, and library trigger.
+- `packages/common/src/editorInterface.ts:142` keeps desktop windows in the full property-panel layout above the phone breakpoint.
+- `excalidraw-app/excalidrawZ/camera.js:275` samples native camera updates while retaining the final value.
+- `excalidraw-app/excalidrawZ/message.js:47` avoids duplicate console bridge messages.
+- `excalidraw-app/App.tsx:398` disables cloud collaboration for the bundled local editor.
+- `excalidraw-app/excalidrawZ/camera.test.js:1` and `desktopControls.test.ts:1` cover sampling and desktop breakpoints.
+
+Build via the host repository's `script/build_release.sh`. The host records this
+editor's base revision plus `patches/editor.patch`; generated assets are not source.
